	(text "MQ-7 heater power switch (low-side, PWM-driven): STM32 timer/GPIO drives Q1\n(2N2222A) as an inverting level shifter -- pin HIGH saturates Q1, pulling Q2's\ngate LOW (MOSFET OFF); pin LOW lets R2 pull Q2's gate to 5V (MOSFET ON).\nR7 (10k) pulls HEATER_CTRL up to +3.3V, so an unconfigured/floating GPIO (e.g.\nbefore firmware runs) reads HIGH by default -- Q1 ON, gate LOW, MOSFET OFF.\nThis IS a true hardware default-off, overridden easily by the GPIO actively\ndriving LOW (any push-pull output sinks far more than R7's 0.33mA).\nFirmware convention -- DEFAULT/idle duty: 72% high / 28% low, averaging 1.4V\non the heater (sense phase, matches the pulled-up HIGH-biased default). On\nthe burn TRIGGER: drive 100% low for 60s for a full 5V (burn phase).\n\nQ1: Collector->gate net, Emitter->GND, Base<-R1<-HEATER_CTRL. Q2: Drain->heater\n(J1 pin 2), Source->GND, Gate<-R2 pull-up/Q1 collector. Both Q1 and Q2 carry a\nschematic mirror (mirror x) so the physical E/C and D/S leads land on the\ncorrect nets -- verify lead order against your actual 2N2222A (TO-92: E-B-C)\nand IRF44N/IRFZ44N (TO-220: G-D-S) datasheets before wiring; package pinouts\nvary by manufacturer.\n\nSensing path: J1 pin 1 (MQ-7 analog output) connects directly to ADC_PA0, no\nscaling divider. CAUTION: if this module's analog VC is 5V, the output can\nexceed the STM32 ADC's 3.3V max -- confirm the module's sensing supply voltage\nbefore relying on this direct connection. Only sample ADC_PA0 during the\nlow/sense phase -- ignore readings taken during the 5V burn phase.\n\nHEATER_CTRL and ADC_PA0 are off-sheet nets to the STM32 GPIO/timer pin and\nADC1 input respectively (MCU not drawn on this sub-circuit sheet)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 187.96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3f39f340-7f0b-4899-a37f-8442eef659dd")
	)
